/	TD8E BOOTSTRAP METHODS.

/	1.	MR8E-C ROM TD8E BOOTSTRAP.

/	ASSUMING THE MR8E-C ROM IS AVAILABLE [WHICH IS A REQUIRMEMENT OF THIS SYSTEM
/	CONFIGURATION], THE FOLLOWING IS THE SHORTEST WAY TO BOOTSTRAP ANY COMPATIBLE
/	TD8E OPERATING SYSTEM [ON LOGICAL UNIT 0 ONLY] BY THE USE OF AN EXECUTABLE
/	PROGRAM.  [USING THE FRONT PANEL SWITCH REGISTER TO BOOTSTRAP THE SYSTEM IS
/	ESSENTIALLY THE MANUAL EQUIVALENT OF THIS PROGRAM.]

	NOPUNCH				/PREVENT BINARY OUTPUT; THIS SECTION IS FOR
					/DOCUMENTATION PURPOSES ONLY.

	*7400				/ANYWHERE ON PAGE 36 OF ANY FIELD.

/	CLA				/THE AC MUST BE CLEAR.
	CIF	70			/GOING TO ROM FIELD.
	JMP	ROMBOOT			/START THE BOOTSTRAP WITHIN THE ROM.

/	NOTE: THIS BOOTSTRAP CAN BE LOADED ON ANY OTHER PAGE BY USING A "JMP I"
/	INSTRUCTION TO ACCESS THE ROM-BASED BOOTSTRAP [WHICH REQUIRES AN ADDITIONAL
/	MEMORY LOCATION FOR THE POINTER ADDRESS].

/	2.	STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP.

	NOPUNCH				/PREVENT BINARY OUTPUT; THIS SECTION IS FOR
					/DOCUMENTATION PURPOSES ONLY.

	FIELD	0			/LOADS IN FIELD 0.

	*7300				/THIS IS WHERE THE STANDALONE BOOTSTRAP LOADS.

K1000,	TAD	GET/(2000)		/GET REVERSE DIRECTION BIT.  ALSO CONSTANT
					/1000 [ONLY THE HIGH-ORDER FOUR BITS ARE USED].
	JMS	GET			/LOCATE REVERSE END ZONE.
	JMS	GET			/LOOK FOR 31 CODE GOING FORWARD.
RD,	SDSQ				/QUAD FLAG UP?
	JMP	.-1			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	SDRD				/YES, READ IT IN.
	DCA I	WCT			/STORE IT INTO MEMORY.
	ISZ	WCT			/BUMP TO NEXT; ALL DONE YET?
	JMP	RD			/NO, KEEP GOING.

/	AT THIS POINT BLOCK 0000 HAS BEEN READ INTO 07360-07557 AND BLOCK 0001 HAS
/	BEEN READ INTO 07600-07777.  [NOTE: ONLY OS/8 AND COS-300/310 REQUIRE THE
/	BLOCK OOO1 DATA LOAD; EDU-SYSTEM 15/30 AND P?S/8 REQUIRE ONLY BLOCK 0000 BE
/	LOADED INTO MEMORY; THE OFFSET WILL BE EXPECTED AND DEALT WITH ACCORDINGLY.]

	JMP I	STRT/(STARTIT)		/GO START IT UP.
/	GET TO DESIRED MARK WINDOW VALUE ROUTINE.  [NOTE: INITIALIZED TO SAVE A WORD.]

GET,	2000				/GET TO DESIRED MARK ROUTINE.
	TAD	K1000/(1000)		/ADD ON UNIT [0] AND GO BITS TO DIRECTION BIT
					/PASSED IN AC.  NOTE: LOW-ORDER BITS IGNORED.
	SDLC				/LOAD COMMAND REGISTER TO START THE TAPE MOVING.
MRKSRCH,SDSS				/NEW LINE IN?
	JMP	.-1			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	SDRC				/YES, READ THE COMMAND REGISTER.
	AND	K77/(77)		/JUST MARK WINDOW BITS.

/	THE FIRST TIME THIS ROUTINE IS USED, THE REVERSE END ZONE MARK VALUE IS BEING
/	SEARCHED FOR; THE SECOND TIME, THE 31 CODE IS BEING SEARCHED FOR.

MARKSEL,TAD	MRKVALUE		/COMPARE TO DESIRED [END MARK OR 31 CODE].
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF IT MATCHES.
	JMP	MRKSRCH			/GO BACK IF NOT.
	ISZ	MARKSEL			/BUMP TO NEXT MARK CODE FOR NEXT TIME.
	JMP I	GET			/RETURN TO CALLER.

WCT,	BOOTBUFFER			/WORD COUNT AND STORE POINTER.

MARKVAL,-22;	-31			/REVERSE END AND 31 CODE MARK CONSTANTS.
K77,	77				/CONSTANT 0077.
STRT,	STARTIT				/WHERE TO START THE BOOT CODE READ IN.

	ZBLOCK	7354-.			/EMPTY SPACE.

	BOOTBUF=.			/DECTAPE BLOCK 0000 CONTENTS START LOADING HERE.

	ZBLOCK	4			/THESE LOCATIONS ARE LOADED WITH PRE-DATA WORDS.

	BLKDATA=.			/THE DATA WORDS FROM BLOCK 0000 LOAD HERE.

	ZBLOCK	7400-.			/THE FIRST 0020 WORDS OF BLOCK 0000 LOAD HERE.

	STARTIT=.			/THE REST OF THE WORDS IN BLOCK 0 LOAD HERE.
					/CONTROL IS TRANSFERRED HERE AFTERWARDS; ALL
					/COMPATIBLE OPERATING SYSTEMS NEED TO BE AWARE
					/OF THIS OFFSET LOADING AND PROVIDE A
					/SYSTEM-SPECIFIC PROCESS TO CONTINUE THE OVERALL
					/LOADING PROCESS.
/	NOTES:

/	1)  THE STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP ALSO LOADS THE CONTENTS OF BLOCK 0001 INTO
/	    07600-07777; THIS IS ONLY MEANINGFUL TO OS/8 AND COS-300/310.

/	2)  THE MR8E-C ROM BOOTSTRAP FUNCTIONS IDENTICALLY TO THE STANDARD DEC TD8E
/	    BOOTSTRAP; CLEARLY THE STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP IS THE TEMPLATE FOR THE
/	    DESIGN OF THE ROM-BASED ROUTINES.

/	3)  THE STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP IS NOT WELL DEVELOPED.  IT CAN BE MADE
/	    MORE ROBUST BY CHANGING THE "K1000" SYMBOLIC REFERENCE TO THE WORD AT
/	    "GET+1" [WHICH WOULD MAKE IT SELF-REFERENTIAL].  THE ONLY REQUIREMENT OF
/	    THE CONSTANT USED IS THE HIGH-ORDER FOUR BITS ARE 0, 0, 1, 0; AS WRITTEN,
/	    EITHER LOCATION ACCOMPLISHES THIS; ONCE THIS CHANGE IS MADE, ADDITIONAL
/	    CHANGES ARE POSSIBLE TO MAKE THIS PROGRAM MORE ROBUST [BY ITSELF, THIS
/	    CHANGE IS MERELY INNOCUOUS].

/	4)  ASSUMING 3) ABOVE HAS BEEN PERFORMED, THE INSTRUCTION AT 07300 CAN BE
/	    CHANGED TO "CLA CLL CML RTR" WHICH LOADS THE ACCUMULATOR WITH 2000 [AKA
/	    "NL2000"].  THIS CHANGE HAS THE ADDED BENEFIT OF ENSURING THE PROPER
/	    CONTENTS OF THE AC AS THE PROGRAM STARTS, WITHOUT RELIANCE ON POWER CLEAR
/	    CONSIDERATIONS [WHICH COULD BE IMPROPERLY CARRIED OUT BY USERS UNFAMILIAR
/	    WITH THE PROCESS].

/	5)  ASSUMING 3) AND 4) ABOVE HAVE BEEN PERFORMED, THE CONTENTS OF "GET" BECOME
/	    UNIMPORTANT.  THIS ALLOWS THE FRONT PANEL OPERATIONS NEEDED TO TOGGLE IN
/	    THIS CODE TO BE ONE OPERATION SHORTER [THE PREVIOUS VALUE CAN BE LEFT ON
/	    THE FRONT PANEL SWITCHES THEN PRESS DEPOSIT TWICE].

/	IT IS CLEAR THIS BOOTSTRAP WAS NOT OPTIMIZED AS IS USUALLY THE CASE WITH OTHER
/	DEC BOOTSTRAPS; HOWEVER, IT IS KNOWN THAT AT THE TIME THE TD8E WAS FIRST
/	PRODUCED, THERE WAS WIDESPREAD PROGRAMMER APATHY OR EVEN OPEN DISDAIN FOR THE
/	DEVICE.  THE NON-ROM VERSION OF A DEVICE HANDLER FOR OS/8 TO SUPPORT THE TD8E
/	[THAT REQUIRES AT LEAST 12K OF MEMORY] IS DOCUMENTED IN SURVIVING OS/8 SOURCE
/	FILES AS "THE TD8E PROBLEM".  THIS ALSO IMPACTED NEGATIVELY ON SUBSEQUENT
/	DEVICE HANDLERS ALSO REQUIRING AT LEAST 12K OF MEMORY; THE HANDLERS FOR THESE
/	NEWER DEVICES WERE PRAGMATICALLY WRITTEN TO SUPERFICIALLY MIMIC QUIRKS OF THE
/	TD8E HANDLER.  THIS BECAME NECESSARY TO ALLOW CERTAIN PROGRAMS TO HANDLE "THE
/	TD8E PROBLEM" GENERICALLY EVEN IF THIS REQUIREMENT WAS DETRIMENTAL TO THE
/	HANDLERS FOR THESE OTHER DEVICES.

/	IT WAS SUGGESTED TO THE PDP-8 PROGRAMMING STAFF THAT OS/8 BE REWRITTEN TO
/	CONFORM TO THE EMERGING P?S/8 MEMORY MANAGEMENT STANDARD USED IN ALL P?S/8
/	RELEASES FROM THAT ERA TO THE PRESENT; THEY CONSIDERED IT A GOOD IDEA BUT TOO
/	MUCH WORK TO BOTHER WITH.  AS SUCH, THE RELEVANT RELEASES OF OS/8 BASIC AND
/	FORTRAN IV HAVE WEAKNESSES WITHIN THEM DIRECTLY TRACEABLE TO THIS "PROBLEM".
/	3.	P?S/8 MULTIPLE UNIT TD8E BOOTSTRAP.

/	THIS BOOTSTRAP IS ONLY FOR P?S/8 SYSTEMS BASED ON THE TD8E DECTAPE CONTROLLER.
/	THE STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP WILL ALSO WORK; HOWEVER, IT CANNOT ACCESS
/	DRIVE UNIT 1 AS AN ALTERNATE BOOTUP DEVICE CHOICE.  [NOTE: IF THE ALTERNATE
/	DRIVE ACCESS FEATURE IS REMOVED, THIS BOOTSTRAP BECOMES ONE WORD SHORTER THAN
/	THE STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP; WITH THE FEATURE PRESENT, IT IS ONE WORD
/	LONGER.]  [NOTE: SUPPORT FOR DRIVE UNIT 1 BOOTUP IN THE P?S/8 TD8E/MR8E-C
/	CONFIGURATION IS CURRENTLY UNDER DEVELOPMENT; IT MAY PROVE IMPOSSIBLE GIVEN
/	THE NEED TO SOLVE THE FATAL FLAW IN THE PRESENT CODE AS WAS RECOVERED FROM
/	THE SPECIFIC DECTAPE IN QUESTION.  THIS BOOTSTRAP MAY BECOME WORTHLESS AS THE
/	FATAL FLAW IS REMOVED, OR PERHAPS MIGHT BE USEFUL WHERE IT IS LIKELY MORE
/	NEEDED, NAMELY ON THE TD8E CONFIGURATION WITH 8K OR MORE WITHOUT THE MR8E-C
/	ROM; FOR THE PRESENT IT IS RETAINED FOR REFERENCE PURPOSES ONLY.]

/	THE STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP IS SELFISHLY DESIGNED TO ALLOW OS/8 BOOTUP
/	EASIER AT THE EXPENSE OF OTHER SYSTEMS COMPATIBLE WITH THIS CONVENTION; AS
/	SUCH, IT IS NEEDLESSLY INFLEXIBLE.  [NUANCES OF OTHER SYSTEMS SUCH AS MULTIPLE
/	DRIVE UNIT SUPPORT CANNOT BE IMPLEMENTED.]

/	THE STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP LOADS THE CONTENTS OF BLOCK 0001 INTO
/	07600-0777 WHERE OS/8 [AND COS-300/310] REQUIRE THIS; THE CONTENTS OF BLOCK
/	0000 ARE LOADED INTO 07360-07557 WHICH IS OF NO PARTICULAR ADVANTAGE TO ANY
/	SUPPORTED SYSTEM [AND TENDS TO CAUSE NEEDLESS BOOTUP COMPLEXITY].  AS SUCH,
/	FOR ALL SUPPORTED SYSTEMS [INCLUDING OS/8 AND COS-300/310], WHATEVER ASPECT OF
/	BLOCK 0000 REQUIRING PROPER PAGE ALIGNMENT [GENERALLY TO 7600-7777, AND IN THE
/	CASES OF OS/8 AND COS-300/310 INTO FIELD 1] IS NOT PROVIDED.  IT IS NECESSARY
/	TO COPY THE CONTENTS OF BLOCK 0 TO THE PROPER MEMORY LOCATIONS VIA ADDITIONAL
/	CODING WITHIN EACH SYSTEMS DEVICE HANDLER STRUCTURE.

/	IN THE CASE OF THE P?S/8 TD8E/MR8E-C SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER, THIS REQUIRES
/	HANDLER CODING TO SUPPORT THE CIRCUMSTANCES OF THIS ODD RELOCATION; MEASURES
/	ARE THEN TAKEN TO UNDO SPECIFIC CORRUPTION CAUSED BY THE MISALIGNMENT.
/	AFTERWARDS, THE HANDLER CODE IS COPIED TO THE INTENDED MEMORY LOCATIONS.  DUE
/	TO THE LIMITATIONS OF THE DEC STANDARD TD8E BOOTSTRAP, ONLY DEVICE UNIT 0 CAN
/	BE ACCESSED AT BOOTUP TIME.

/	THE P?S/8-SPECIFIC BOOTSTRAP CORRECTS THESE PROBLEMS BY PROPERLY LOADING THE
/	ENTIRE BLOCK 0000 CONTENTS DIRECTLY INTO 07600-07777 AS INTENDED.  THIS WILL
/	ALLOW FUTURE RELEASES TO POTENTIALLY SUPPORT BOOTING TO DRIVE UNIT 1
/	[ASSUMING PROPER REVISIONS ARE MADE TO ALL AFFECTED COMPONENTS].

/	NOTE: THE BUILT-IN BOOTSTRAP WITHIN THE MR8E-C ROM IS CONSISTENT WITH THE
/	DEC STANDARD TD8E BOOTSTRAP IN ALL RELEVANT WAYS.  ONLY THE P?S/8 TD8E
/	BOOTSTRAP HAS THE POTENTIAL TO ACCESS DRIVE UNIT 1.
	NOPUNCH				/PREVENT BINARY OUTPUT; THIS SECTION IS FOR
					/DOCUMENTATION PURPOSES ONLY.

	*7542				/STARTING ADDRESS OF BOOT CODE.

/	NOTE: THE FIRST WORD BELOW NEED NOT BE LOADED INTO MEMORY IF THE BOOTSTRAP
/	PROGRAM IS STARTED AT 07560.  IT IS PROVIDED SO THAT THE STARTING AND LOWEST
/	LOADING ADDRESS ARE IDENTICAL TO MINIMIZE THE INFORMATION NEEDED FOR AN
/	AVERAGE USER TO SUCCESSFULLY START P?S/8 FOR THE TD8E.  [NOTE: IT IS HOPED
/	THIS BOOTSTRAP WILL BE COMPATIBLE WITH THE P?S/8 TD8E CONFIGURATION FOR USE
/	WITH 8K OR LARGER SYSTEMS THAT DO NOT INCLUDE THE MR8E-C ROM.]

GTMARK,	JMP	BUTSTRT			/JUMP TO REAL START.
GT1000,	TAD	GT1000/(1000)		/ADD ON UNIT 0, GO BIT TO PASSED DIRECTION.
	SDLC				/LOAD COMMAND REGISTER TO START THE TAPE MOVING.
GTSRCH,	SDSS				/NEW LINE IN?
	JMP	.-1			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	SDRC				/YES, READ THE COMMAND REGISTER.
	AND	GT77/(77)		/JUST MARK TRACK BITS.
TADGTCM,TAD	GTCMPVALUE		/GET END MARK [OR 31 MARK] COMPARISON VALUE.
	SZA CLA				/SKIP IF IT MATCHES.
	JMP	GTSRCH			/GO BACK IF NO MATCH.
	ISZ	TADGTCMP		/LOOK FOR 31 CODE SECOND TIME THROUGH.
	JMP I	GTMARK			/RETURN TO CALLER.

GTCT,	SBOOT-4				/WORD COUNT AND STORE POINTER.
GSBTFUN,SBTFUN				/POINTER TO SBTFUN.

/	THE BOOTSTRAP STARTS HERE [OR IS BRANCHED TO FROM THE LOWEST LOADING ADDRESS].

BUTSTRT,NL2000				/SET REVERSE DIRECTION BIT.
	JMS	GTMARK			/REWIND TAPE 0 INTO THE END ZONE.
	JMS	GTMARK			/READ FORWARD TO 31 MARK.
GTLOOP,	SDSQ				/QUAD LINE FLAG UP?
	JMP	.-1			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	SDRD				/YES, GET A WORD.
	DCA I	GTCT			/STORE INTO BOOT AREA.
	ISZ	GTCT			/DONE ENOUGH?
	JMP	GTLOOP			/NO, GO DO ANOTHER ONE.

/	SET THE P?S/8 BOOTSTRAP LOGICAL UNIT.

	ISZ I	GSBTFUN/(SBTFUN)	/BOOT TO DRIVE 1.

	*.-1				/GO BACK.

	NOP				/BOOT TO DRIVE 0.

	DCA	SB7577			/LAST WORD ON THE PAGE BECOMES. "AND 0000".
	JMP	SB7577			/GO THERE TO FALL INTO THE BOOTUP ROUTINE.
/	AS THE BLOCK 0000 DATA IS READ IN, THE NEXT FOUR WORDS ARE REPLACED WITH THE
/	CONTENTS OF WORDS PRIOR TO THE DATA WORDS OF BLOCK 0000.  THIS OVERLAY IS
/	ALLOWED BECAUSE THE STATED CONTENTS ARE ONLY ACCESSED PRIOR TO THE DATA
/	TRANSFER.

/	THE CONTENTS OF 07577 ARE CLEARED BEFORE THE PROGRAM TRANSFERS CONTROL THERE.
/	THE LOCATION WILL EXECUTE AS A HARMLESS "AND 0000" INSTRUCTION; EXECUTION
/	CONTINUES BY FALLING THROUGH INTO LOCATION 07600 WHICH IS THE STANDARD RESTART
/	ADDRESS OF P?S/8.

GTCMPVA,-22				/REVERSE END ZONE MARK CONSTANT.
	-31				/31 CODE MARK CONSTANT.
GT77,	77				/CONSTANT 0077.

/	THE NEXT WORD DOES NOT HAVE TO BE LOADED; IT IS ONLY STORED INTO.

SB7577,	.-.				/LOCATION 07577; THE CONTENTS WILL BE REPLACED
					/WITH 0000 WHICH EXECUTES AS "AND 0000".

/	THE CODE FALLS THROUGH INTO THE BOOTUP CODE READ IN FROM THE DECTAPE.  AS
/	APPROPRIATE, THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER MAY BE MODIFIED TO BOOT TO DRIVE UNIT 1
/	[ASSUMING THIS IS SUPPORTED].

	SBOOT=	.			/SYSTEM BOOTS HERE.

	ENPUNCH				/RESTORE NORMAL BINARY OUTPUT.

/	NOTE: THIS BOOTSTRAP MAY NOT BE FEASIBLE DEPENDING ON THE INTERNALS OF THE
/	P?S/8 TD8E HANDLER WHICH IS UNDERGOING DESIGN CHANGES; HOWEVER, IT IS
/	CONCEIVABLE THAT ELEMENTS OF THIS BOOTSTRAP MAY BECOME RELEVANT TO THE NON-ROM
/	CONFIGURATION.
/	TD8E/MR8E-C DECTAPE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER.

	FIELD	0			/WHERE THIS LOADS WHEN GENERATED/EXECUTED.

	*GENAD1				/REQUIRED FOR SYSTEM GENERATION PURPOSES.

	RELOC	SBOOT			/WHERE THE CODE EXECUTES.

SBOOT,	JMS	SYSIO			/CALL SYSTEM I/O ROUTINES TO BOOTUP.
	SBOOT				/READ INTO 07600 AND ONWARD.
SBTFUN,	20^100+.-.			/FUNCTION WORD; LOW-ORDER UNIT BIT MAY BE SET.
	SYSBLK				/BLOCK 0000 AND ONWARD.

/	ALTHOUGH SEEMINGLY A SUBROUTINE CALL, THERE IS NO ACTUAL RETURN TO THE CALLER.
/	ONCE INITIATED, DATA TRANSFERS OVERLAY MEMORY; KEY CONTROLLING ADDRESSES AND
/	OTHER PARAMETERS READ IN FROM BLOCK 0000 TAKE CONTROL OF THE OVERALL PROCESS
/	IN MEMORY.  THE ACTUAL TRANSFER IS 07600-03577 [USING ADDRESS WRAP-AROUND
/	KNOWN TO CONTINUE IN FIELD 0].  THE FUNCTION WORD IS SET TO READ 20 BLOCKS
/	INTO MEMORY [BLOCKS 0000-0017].  THIS INITIALIZES THE KEYBOARD MONITOR [AND
/	BUILT-IN LINE EDITOR], THE RESIDENT COPY OF THE TFS DIRECTORY AND THE KEYBOARD
/	MONITOR TRANSIENT COMMAND AREA.  [NOTE: FINALIZATION OF THESE SYSTEM
/	COMPONENTS IS PERFORMED WITHIN THE KEYBOARD MONITOR.]

/	ONCE COMPLETELY LOADED [AND MOVED BY THE KEYBOARD MONITOR FOR CERTAIN AREAS]
/	THE MEMORY LAYOUT IS AS FOLLOWS:

 /	BLOCK[S]	  MEMORY	FUNCTION

/	  0000		07600-07777	THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER.

/	0001-0014	00000-02777	THE RESIDENT KEYBOARD MONITOR AND LINE EDITOR.

/	   N/A		03000-06777	INTERNAL FILE BUFFER FOR THE LINE EDITOR.

/	0015-0016	07000-07377	CACHED COPY OF THE CURRENT UNIT TFS DIRECTORY.

/	  0017		07400-07577	THE TRANSIENT AREA OF THE KEYBOARD MONITOR.

/	NOTE: THE TRANSIENT AREA SERVES SEVERAL PURPOSES.  THE CONTENTS AND USAGE
/	DEPENDS ON VARIOUS COMMANDS.

SWAL,	.-.				/COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCHES '/A'-'/L'.
SWMX,	.-.				/COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCHES '/M'-'/X'.
SWY9,	.-.				/COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCHES '/Y'-'/9'.
SOUTFLS,2316/.-.			/OUTPUT FILE COUNT ETC. WORD.
SDATE,	2316/.-.			/SYSTEM DATE WORD.
SCRSIZE,4000/.-.			/SYSTEM CORE SIZE.
/	NOTES ON OUTPUT FILE COUNT, SYSTEM DATE AND SYSTEM CORE SIZE WORDS:

/	THE OUTPUT FILE COUNT WORD WILL BE REDEFINED IN P?S/8 VERSION 9A.  AS OF
/	VERSION 8Z, BITS[7-11] CONTAIN THE COUNT OF OUTPUT FILES IN THE PASSED FILE
/	LIST; HOWEVER, BITS[0-6] MUST BE 0000000.  BITS[1-6] WILL BECOME THE
/	HIGH-ORDER SIX BITS OF A REDESIGNED DATE WORD THAT COVERS 512 YEARS DIRECTLY.
/	BIT[0] WILL DETERMINE THE STATUS OF THE FILE AND COMMUNICATIONS AREA OF THE
/	OPTIONAL P?S/8 SHELL [CURRENTLY UNDER DEVELOPMENT].  AS SUCH, ALL CONFORMING
/	PROGRAMS MUST MASK OFF BITS[0-6] TO OBTAIN THE OUTPUT FILE COUNT.

/	THE FORMAT OF THE SYSTEM DATE WORD WILL BE MODIFIED TO FORM AN 18-BIT INTEGER
/	WHEN COMBINED WITH BITS[1-6] OF THE OUTPUT FILE COUNT WORD.  THIS WILL REQUIRE
/	ALL PROGRAMS THAT ACCESS THE SYSTEM DATE TO BE REWRITTEN.  THIS IS ALSO
/	SCHEDULED FOR IMPLEMENTATION IN P?S/8 VERSION 9A.

/	THE CORE SIZE WORD CONTAINS SEVERAL SETS OF MEMORY AND OTHER STATUS BITS:

/	BITS[0-2] CONTAIN THE PHYSICAL SIZE OF MEMORY OF THE SYSTEM.

/	BITS[3-5] CONTAIN THE MAXIMUM SIZE THE LOGICAL CORE SIZE CAN BE SET TO.  THIS
/	COULD DIFFER FROM THE PHYSICAL SIZE FOR SEVERAL REASONS SUCH AS THE PRESENCE
/	OF THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IN THE PHYSICAL MAXIMUM FIELD, OR THE SYSTEM
/	DEVICE HANDLER REQUIRES AN EXTENSION SUCH AS IN THE CASE OF THE TD8E SYSTEM
/	THAT REQUIRES 8K OF MEMORY OR MORE [BUT DOES NOT USE THE MR8E-C ROM].

/	BITS[6-8] CONTAIN THE CURRENT LOGICAL CORE SIZE.  THIS VALUE CAN BE SET TO
/	ANY VALUE FROM 0 UP THROUGH THAT FOUND IN THE MAXIMUM LOGICAL SIZE STORED IN
/	BITS[3-5].  THIS ALLOWS PROGRAMS TO BE TESTED IN RESTRICTED CONFIGURATIONS TO
/	MIMIC THE LIMITATIONS OF SMALLER MACHINES OR TO PROTECT THE CONTENTS OF MEMORY
/	FOR USER-DEFINED PURPOSES.

/	BIT[9] IS SET IF THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER REQUIRES A DEVICE EXTENSION.  THE
/	DEVICE EXTENSION OCCUPIES LOCATIONS 6000-7777 OF THE HIGHEST PHYSICAL FIELD OF
/	MEMORY.  [NOTE: CERTAIN SYSTEM PROGRAMS SUCH AS P?S/8 PAL CAN ALLOCATE
/	LOCATIONS 0000-5777 OF THE HIGHEST PHYSICAL FIELD IN CASE THE LOGICAL CONSOLE
/	IS DISABLED AND THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER REQUIRES THE EXTENSION.]

/	BIT[10] IS SET IF THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS ACTIVE.  ENTRY POINTS ARE
/	IMPLIED WITH RESPECT TO SPECIFIC 12-BIT ADDRESSES; THE FIELD IS DEFINED AS ONE
/	FIELD MORE THAN THE FIELD VALUE IN BITS[3-5].  WHILE THIS IS GENERALLY
/	IDENTICAL TO THE FIELD REPRESENTED BY THE PHYSICAL CORE SIZE, THIS METHOD
/	ALLOWS MULTIPLE MEMORY FIELDS TO BE RESERVED FOR UNUSUAL CONFIGURATIONS.

/	BIT[11] IS THE LOGICAL ABORT SWITCH THAT ANY PROGRAM CAN SET TO SIGNAL PROGRAM
/	EXIT BY ABORT [GENERALLY CONTROL-C DETECTED ON THE SYSTEM CONSOLE DEVICE].
/	WHILE COMPATIBLE PDP-8 CONSOLE HARDWARE CAN PROVIDE THIS INFORMATION VIA THE
/	KEYBOARD FLAG BEING RAISED [AND THE KEYBOARD BUFFER CONTAINING THE CONTROL-C
/	CHARACTER], DECMATES ARE NOT CAPABLE OF THIS DUE TO THE INCOMPATIBLE KEYBOARD
/	HARDWARE ON ALL MODELS.  BY SETTING BIT[11] AS NECESSARY, FULLY CONFORMING
/	PROGRAMS CAN BE WRITTEN TO COMPLETELY FUNCTION ON ALL PDP-8 AND DECMATE MODELS
/	SUPPORTED.  [NOTE: P?S/8 ONLY SUPPORTS "FAMILY OF 8" MODELS WHICH EXPLICITLY
/	EXCLUDE THE PDP-5 AND PDP-8/S; THESE MACHINES ARE NOT COMPATIBLE WITH THE
/	ORIGINAL PDP-8 MODEL RELEASED IN 1965 WHICH IS CONSIDERED THE MINIMUM SYSTEM
/	THAT CAN BE SUPPORTED IN P?S/8 AND ALSO OS/8 WITH SUFFICIENT MEMORY.]
/	COMES HERE WITH INTERRUPTS OFF TO CONTINUE PROCESSING THE LATEST SYSTEM DEVICE
/	HANDLER CALL.

SMORE,	RDF				/GET THE CALLER'S FIELD.
	TAD	SCIDF/(CIF CDF)		/TURN INTO CIF CDF RETURN FIELD INSTRUCTION.
	DCA	SFLDXIT			/STORE INLINE FOR EXIT LATER.
	TAD I	SYSIO			/GET THE CALLER'S BUFFER ADDRESS.
	DCA	BUFADRESS		/STASH IT FOR THE ROM ROUTINES.
	ISZ	SYSIO			/BUMP TO FUNCTION WORD.

/	NOTE: THE FOLLOWING INSTRUCTIONS ARE EXECUTED IN LOCATIONS 07400 ONWARD DURING
/	THE STANDARD DEC TD8E [OR ROM-BASED] BOOTSTRAP; THE EFFECTS OF THIS WILL BE
/	INDICATED IN THE COMMENTS ON THE MISALIGNED CODE AFTER THE NORMAL USAGE BELOW.

	SDLC				/STOP THE TAPE NOW.  [SEEMINGLY EXTRANEOUS.]
	NL7776				/MASK THE UNIT BIT OFF.
	AND I	SYSIO			/GET ALL OTHER FUNCTION WORD BITS.
	SDLD				/LOAD DATA REGISTER TO CONFORM WITH THE ROM.
	AND	S70/(70)		/GET BACK FIELD BITS FOR CALLER'S BUFFER.
	TAD	SCIDF/(CIF CDF)		/FORM "CIF CDF" INSTRUCTION TO CALLER'S BUFFER
					/FIELD.  NOTE: THE "CIF" IS EXTRANEOUS BECAUSE
					/THE INSTRUCTION FIELD WILL BE CHANGED TO 7.
	DCA	GETFLD			/STORE INTO "GETWRD" ROUTINE.
	TAD	GETFLD			/GET IT BACK.
	DCA	PUTFLD			/ALSO STORE INTO "PUTWRD" ROUTINE.
/	TAD I	SYSTEM			/GET THE FUNCTION WORD AGAIN.
	JMP	SMORE2			/CONTINUE THERE.

/	THE FOLLOWING IS WHAT OCCURS WHEN THE ABOVE WORDS ARE LOCATED AT 07400 ONWARD
/	BECAUSE OF THE STANDARD DEC TD8E [OR ROM-BASED] BOOTSTRAP.

/	*7400				/WHERE THESE WORDS EXECUTE.

/	DECTAPE DRIVE UNIT 0 IS STILL MOVING FROM THE LAST BOOTUP DATA TRANSFER.

/	SDLC				/THE AC IS CLEAR; STOP THE DRIVE.
/	NL7776				/AC SET TO 7776.
/	AND I	SYSIO&177+7420/(5654)	/MASK AGAINST THE RANDOM CONTENTS OF 05654.
/	SDLD				/PUT JUNK VALUE INTO THE DATA REGISTER.
/	AND	S70&177+7420/(5625)	/MASK OFF SOME BITS.
/	TAD	S6203&177+7420/(2353)	/ADD WORTHLESS CONSTANT.
/	DCA	GETFLD&177+7420		/DESTROY "SROMGO" POINTER.
/	TAD	GETFLD&177+7420		/GET JUNK VALUE BACK.
/	DCA	PUTFLD&177+7420		/DESTROY "WRQUAD" ROUTINE RETURN INSTRUCTION.

/	THE DECTAPE DRIVE HAS CORRECTLY BEEN STOPPED; HOWEVER, TWO LOCATIONS OF THE
/	HANDLER HAVE BEEN DESTROYED.  THIS DAMAGE MUST BE REPAIRED BEFORE THE HANDLER
/	IS SAFE TO MOVE TO THE PROPER LOCATIONS.

/	JMP	SMORE2&177+7420		/CONTINUE IN DAMAGE RECOVERY ROUTINE.

	ZBLOCK	7632-.			/EMPTY SPACE [IF ANY].
/	THE SYSTEM LOADER STARTS HERE. VARIOUS ARGUMENTS ARE STORED AS NECESSARY TO
/	IMPLEMENT A VARIETY OF SPECIFIC TASKS [SUCH AS STARTING A SYSTEM PROGRAM OR
/	IMPLEMENTING SYSTEM PROGRAM OVERLAYS].

/	THE DEFAULT CONTENTS WILL SAVE ALL OF FIELD 0 IN BLOCKS 0020-0057 [WHICH IS
/	ALSO THE BLOCKS OF THE TWO FILES "%" [0020-0037] AND "$" [0040-0057]
/	RESPECTIVELY.  THIS DEFINES HOW CORE-IMAGES ARE HANDLED WITHIN P?S/8 WHEN
/	USING SUCH PROGRAMS AS "GET", "START", "ODT" AND "BSAVE".  THE CORE IMAGE MAY
/	ALSO BE MOVED TO TWO DESIGNATED TINY FILE SYSTEM [TFS] FILES TO DEFER SUCH
/	WORK TO A LATER TIME WHEN THE TWO FILES ARE RESTORED.  WHEN THE "GET" COMMAND
/	[OR EQUIVALENT] IS USED, THE PROGRAM STARTING ADDRESS IS 07632 TO IMPLEMENT
/	THIS DEFAULT ACTION.

SLOAD,	JMS	SYSIO			/SYSTEM LOADER ENTRY POINT; DEFAULT VALUES
					/SAVE ALL OF FIELD 0 THEN RESTART.
SCORE,	0000				/BUFFER STARTING ADDRESS; DEFAULT VALUE
					/IS LOCATION 00000. 
SFUN,	00^100+WRITE+.-.		/FUNCTION WORD; DEFAULT IS WRITE 40 BLOCKS FROM
					/THE FIELD 0 BUFFER [LOCATIONS 00000-07777].
					/AS REQUIRED, THE LOGICAL UNIT BITS WILL BE
					/FILLED IN TO INDICATE THE BOOTUP UNIT.
SBLOCK,	BINADR				/STARTING BLOCK NUMBER; DEFAULT IS 0020.
	JMP I	.+1/(SYSTART)		/START AT THE INDICATED STARTING ADDRESS.
SYSTART,SBOOT				/STARTING ADDRESS; DEFAULTS TO THE SYSTEM
					/RESTART ADDRESS.

/	THE DEVICE HANDLER I/O ROUTINES ENTER HERE.  THE CALLER MUST SET THE DATA
/	FIELD TO THE CALLING FIELD; THE CONTENTS OF THE AC AND LINK ARE IGNORED WHEN
/	ENTERED.  UPON RETURN THE AC WILL BE CLEAR; THE LINK CONTENTS ARE GENERALLY
/	NOT MEANINGFUL; HOWEVER, MOST P?S/8 SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLERS ALSO CLEAR THE LINK
/	[IF POSSIBLE].

/	SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER ENTRY POINT.

/	THIS ABSOLUTELY *MUST* BE AT LOCATION 07640.

	IFNZRO	SZA CLA-. <ERROR .>	/ENSURE ENTRY POINT MATCHES "SZA CLA" VALUE.

SYSIO,	2530/MONSTRT			/SYSTEM HANDLER ENTRY POINT.  INITIALIZED FOR
					/THE BOOTSTRAP TO STARTUP THE KEYBOARD MONITOR.
	CLA CLL IAC			/CLEAR THE LINK AND SET AC TO 0001.
S6000,	SKON				/SKIP THE NEXT IF INTERRUPTS ARE ON AND
					/ALSO TURN THE INTERRUPT SYSTEM OFF.
	IAC				/AC=1 IF INTERRUPTS WERE ON, AC=2 IF
					/INTERRUPTS WERE OFF.
	TAD	S6000/(IOF-2)		/NOW HAVE "IOF" INSTRUCTION IF INTERRUPTS WERE
					/OFF OR "ION" INSTRUCTION IF INTERRUPTS WERE ON
					/BEFORE THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER WAS CALLED.
	DCA	SINTXIT			/STORE IN LINE FOR EXIT LATER.
	JMP	SMORE			/CONTINUE THERE.
/	SUPPORT ROUTINES FOR THE ROM-BASED CODE; THIS CODE CANNOT BE MOVED.

GETWRD,	.-.				/GET A WORD FROM THE CALLER'S BUFFER ROUTINE.
GETFLD,	.-.^10+CDF			/WILL BE "CIF CDF XX" WHERE XX IS THE
					/DATA FIELD OF THE CALLER'S BUFFER.
	TAD I	BUFPTR			/GET A WORD FROM THE BUFFER.
	CIF	ROMFLD			/GOING TO ROM FIELD.
	JMP I	GETWRD			/RETURN TO CALLER.

PUTWRD,	READLP+6			/PUT A WORD INTO THE CALLER'S BUFFER ROUTINE.
					/THIS WORD IS INITIALIZED FOR DIRECT OVERLAY
					/DURING THE BOOTUP OPERATION [PRESENTLY].
PUTFLD,	.-.^10+CDF			/WILL BE "CIF CDF XX" WHERE XX IS THE
					/DATA FIELD OF THE CALLER'S BUFFER.
	DCA I	BUFPTR			/PUT A WORD INTO THE BUFFER.
	CIF	ROMFLD			/GOING TO ROM FIELD.
	JMP I	PUTWRD			/RETURN TO CALLER.

/	ROM-DETECTED DECTAPE ERRORS COME HERE.

SERR,	CLA CLL				/ENSURE LINK IS CLEAR FOR RETRIES.
	HLT				/HALT ON ALL ERRORS.
	CIF	ROMFLD			/GOING TO ROM FIELD.
	JMP I	SROMGO/(ROMGO)		/RETRY THE LATEST BLOCK.

/	CALL HANDLING CONTINUES HERE.

/	BY PASSING THE LOGICAL UNIT BIT DIRECTLY TO THIS PART OF THE ROM SETUP CODE,
/	THE RETRY COUNTER SUPPORT IS BYPASSED [ALLOWING THE RETRY COUNTER WORD TO BE
/	REPURPOSED].  [LOOK IN THE OS/8 HANDLER FOR HOW TO INTERACT WITH THE RETRY
/	COUNTER; THIS MAKES TAPE OPERATIONS LESS RELIABLE COMPARED TO P?S/8.]

SMORE3,	TAD	SUNIT			/GET LOGICAL DRIVE UNIT.
	CIF	ROMFLD			/GOING TO ROM FIELD.
	JMP I	SF2SET5/(F2SET+5)	/CONTINUE SETUP THERE IN THE ROM.

/	NOTE: THE FOLLOWING WORD IS SUBJECT TO DESTRUCTION WHEN THE CONTENTS OF BLOCK
/	0000 ARE LOADED INTO 07360-07557.  THE RECOVERY ROUTINE WILL HAVE TO RECREATE
/	THE PROPER CONTENTS PRIOR TO MOVING THE ENTIRE PAGE CONTENTS FROM 07360-07557
/	TO 07600-07777; THIS CAN BE AVOIDED BY ONE OF SEVERAL METHODS:

/	1)  REWORK THE CODE NORMALLY LOADED AT 07620 TO AVOID THE DESTRUCTION [AND
/	    HOPEFULLY NOT MERELY CAUSE SOME ALTERNATE DESTRUCTION].

/	2)  REPURPOSE THE LOCATION TO BECOME AN UNIMPORTANT VALUE [OR COMPLETELY
/	    UNREFERENCED] THUS THE DESTRUCTION WOULD BECOME SUPERFLUOUS.

SROMGO,	ROMGO				/POINTER TO "ROMGO" ROUTINE TO START SEARCH.
/	NOTE: THE PREVIOUS FOUR WORDS MAY BE REWORKED INTO THE FOLLOWING:

/S70,	70				/CONSTANT 0070.
/SROMGO,ROMGO				/POINTER TO "ROMGO" ROUTINE TO START SEARCH.

/	ZBLOCK	1			/EMPTY SPACE THAT MAY BE USEFUL.

/	ZBLOCK	1			/EMPTY SPACE THAT CAN BE HARMLESSLY DESTROYED.

WRQUAD,	.-.				/WRITE A 12-BIT WORD TO THE DECTAPE ROUTINE.

/	THE ACTUAL CODE IS IN THE ROM; THIS IS USED ONLY TO ESTABLISH THE PROPER
/	SUBROUTINE LINKAGE AS IT IS CALLED FROM SEVERAL PLACES.

	CIF	ROMFLD			/GOING TO THE ROM FIELD.
	JMP	WRQ			/CONTINUE THERE.

/	COMES BACK HERE FROM THE ROM-BASED CODE THAT CARRIES OUT THE SUBROUTINE CODE.

CIFR,	CIF	ROMFLD			/GOING TO THE ROM FIELD.
	JMP I	WRQUAD			/RETURN TO CALLER.

/	NOTE: THE PREVIOUS WORD IS SUBJECT TO DESTRUCTION WHEN THE CONTENTS OF BLOCK
/	0000 ARE LOADED INTO 07360-07557.  THE RECOVERY ROUTINE WILL HAVE TO RECREATE
/	THE PROPER CONTENTS PRIOR TO MOVING THE ENTIRE PAGE CONTENTS FROM 07360-07557
/	TO 07600-07777; THIS CAN ONLY BE AVOIDED BY REWORKING THE CODE THAT STARTS UP
/	AT 07400 [NORMALLY IN 07620 ONWARD] IF POSSIBLE.  WHILE THIS IS UNLIKELY, IT
/	SHOULD BE POSSIBLE TO ALLOW THE RECOVERY ROUTINE TO FIT INTO THE ALLOTED CODE
/	SPACE AND ALSO REBOOT THE SYSTEM BY AN ALTERNATE METHOD DESCRIBED BELOW WHILE
/	STILL RESTORING THE PREVIOUS WORD.  [CODE SPACE CAN BE OBTAINED BY OTHER
/	RELATED METHODS IN A VIABLE OVERALL SOLUTION.]

RDQUAD,	.-.				/READ A 12-BIT WORD FROM THE DECTAPE ROUTINE.
	SDSQ				/QUAD LINE FLAG UP?
	JMP	.-1			/NO, WAIT FOR IT.
	SDRD				/YES, READ IN THE LATEST 12-BIT WORD.
	CIF	ROMFLD			/GOING TO ROM FIELD.
	JMP I	RDQUAD			/RETURN TO CALLER.

EQUFUN,	6364/.-.			/EQUIVALENCE DATA WITH CHECKSUM ROUTINE.
	CMA				/INVERT THE DATA AND ,XOR. THE DATA WORD.
	DCA	EQUTMP			/SAVE IT.
	TAD	EQUTMP			/GET IT BACK.
	AND	SCKSUM			/GET THE CARRY BITS.
	CIA				/INVERT FOR SUBTRACTION.
	CLL RAL				/MOVE OVER.
	TAD	EQUTMP			/NOW ADD THE LATEST.
	TAD	SCKSUM			/ADD THE NON-CARRY BITS TO RUNNING SUM.
	DCA	SCKSUM			/STORE BACK.
	TAD	EQUTMP			/GET THE LATEST DATA BACK.
	CLL CMA				/NOW HAVE CLEAR LINK AND THE LATEST WORD.
	CIF	ROMFLD			/GOING TO ROM FIELD.
	JMP I	EQUFUN			/RETURN TO CALLER.
/	THE ROM CODE RETURNS HERE WHEN ALL TAPE OPERATIONS HAVE FINISHED.

SEXIT,	TAD	SUNIT			/GET LATEST DRIVE UNIT.
	SDLC				/STOP THE TAPE DRIVE.

/	RESTORE INTERRUPT STATUS PRIOR TO THE DEVICE HANDLER CALL.

SINTXIT,IOF				/OR ION.
SFLDXIT,CIF CDF	00			/WILL BE "CIF CDF" TO CALLER'S FIELD.
/	ISZ	SYSIO			/BUMP PAST BLOCK ARGUMENT.
	JMP I	SYSIO			/RETURN TO CALLER.

S70,	70				/CONSTANT 0070.
					/NOTE: THIS CONSTANT COULD BE MOVED TO ALLOW
					/THE "ISZ SYSIO" INSTRUCTION IN THIS SECTION.

/	ALTHOUGH THE ROM-BASED CODE SETS UP A RETRY COUNTER, THE P?S/8 DEVICE HANDLER
/	DOESN'T USE IT.  BY AVOIDANCE OF THAT SECTION OF THE ROM SETUP CODE, THE
/	LOCATION CAN BE REPURPOSED.

	TRYCNT=	.			/USED AS AN ERROR RETRY COUNT IN OTHER SYSTEMS.

SF2SET5,F2SET+5				/POINTER TO ROM-BASED SETUP WITHOUT RETRY COUNT.
DRVUNIT,0^4000				/ROM COPIES "SUNIT" HERE [REDUNDANT DATA].
SFUNCTI,0^4000				/FUNCTION WORD BIT[0]; CLEAR=READ, SET=WRITE.
					/[NOTE: ALL OTHER BITS ARE IGNORED.]
SCKSUM,	0/.-.				/RUNNING CHECKSUM WORD.
SBLK,	0000				/LATEST DECTAPE BLOCK.
SUNIT,	0^4000				/DRIVE UNIT FOR LATEST FUNCTION IN BIT[0].

/	COMES HERE TO CONTINUE THE HANDLER CALL.

SMORE2,	TAD I	SYSIO			/GET THE FUNCTION WORD AGAIN.
					/NOTE: THE PREVIOUS WORD MAY BE MOVABLE.
	RAR				/UNIT BIT TO LINK.
	CLA RAR				/UNIT BIT NOW IN AC[0].
	DCA	SUNIT			/SET THE DRIVE UNIT FOR ROM.
	ISZ	SYSIO			/BUMP PAST FUNCTION WORD.
	TAD I	SYSIO			/GET STARTING BLOCK NUMBER FOR TRANSFER.
	DCA	SBLK			/STORE IT.
	ISZ	SYSIO			/BUMP PAST BLOCK ARGUMENT.
					/NOTE: THE PREVIOUS WORD MAY BE REMOVABLE.
SCIDF,	CIF CDF	00			/GOING TO FIELD 0; ALSO CONSTANT 6203.
	JMP	SMORE3			/CONTINUE THERE.

/	NOTE: THE "JMP SMORE3" ABOVE COULD BE REMOVED; THE CODE AT "SMORE3" COULD BE
/	PLACED HERE IF OTHER CHANGES THROUGHOUT THE HANDLER ARE MADE.

/	TAD	SUNIT			/GET LOGICAL DRIVE UNIT.
/	CIF	ROMFLD			/GOING TO ROM FIELD.
/	JMP I	SF2SET5/(F2SET+5)	/CONTINUE SETUP THERE IN THE ROM.
EQUTMP,	0/.-.				/TEMPORARY FOR EQUIVALENCE ROUTINE.
BUFADRE,SBOOT/.-.			/READ/WRITE BUFFER POINTER.
PAGCNT,	20^200/.-.			/TRANSFER PAGE COUNT.
BUFPTR,	./.-.				/BUFFER POINTER FOR WORD TRANSFERS.
WORDCT,	./.-.				/WORD COUNTER FOR LATEST BLOCK TRANSFER.
/	ROMGO				/THIS CAN USED BY THE RECOVERY ROUTINE OR HELP
					/AVOID THE NEED TO RECOVER A CONSTANT.
/	NOTE: THE CODE CAN BE REWORKED TO USE THE ADDRESS CONSTANT ABOVE DIRECTLY.

	ZBLOCK	7756-.			/EMPTY SPACE.

	SPARM=	.			/=XXXX PARAMETER PASSED HERE.

	SFILES=	.+1			/FILE LIST PASSED HERE THROUGH 07777.

/	THE CONTENTS OF THIS AREA IS THE RECOVERY ROUTINE THAT IS LOADED WITH THE SAME
/	OFFSET AS THE ROUTINE THAT CAUSED THE DESTRUCTION OF TWO WORDS.  THIS IS DUE
/	TO THE OFFSET APPLIED EARLIER [AT 07400 AND FOLLOWING INSTEAD OF THE NORMAL
/	07620].

/	*7356				/WHERE THIS CODE IS WHEN OFFSET LOADED.

	CLA CLL				/CLEAN UP.
	SDLC				/STOP THE TAPE.

/	NOTE: THE PREVIOUS TWO INSTRUCTIONS ARE REDUNDANT AS THE AC IS ALREADY CLEAR
/	AND THE TAPE WAS STOPPED EARLIER.  IF THE CODE THAT STARTS AT 07400 IS CHANGED
/	TO REMOVE THE "SDLC" THERE, IT WOULD BE NECESSARY TO RETAIN IT HERE.

	TAD	S7405-20/(ROMGO)	/GET A COPY OF THE DESTROYED VALUE.
	DCA	SROMGO-20		/PUT IT BACK.
	TAD	S5671-20/(JMP I WRQUAD)	/GET A COPY OF THE DESTROYED VALUE.
	DCA	CIFR+1-20		/PUT IT BACK.
SMVLUP,	TAD I	SFROM-20		/GET A WORD.
	DCA I	STO-20			/PUT A WORD.
	ISZ	SFROM-20		/BUMP TO NEXT WORD TO MOVE.
	ISZ	STO-20			/BUMP POINTER/COUNTER.
	JMP	SMVLUP-20		/KEEP GOING UNTIL ALL ARE MOVED.
	JMP I	S7600-20		/GO START UP A COMPLETE REBOOT.

/	THE CODE ABOVE ACTUALLY EXECUTES AS DEFINED IN THE COMMENTS BELOW.

/	TAD	S7405&177+7420		/GET A COPY OF THE DESTROYED VALUE.
/	DCA	GETFLD&177+7420		/PUT IT BACK.
/	TAD	S5671&177+7420		/GET A COPY OF THE DESTROYED VALUE.
/	DCA	PUTFLD&177+7420		/PUT IT BACK.
/SMVLUP,TAD I	SFROM&177+7420		/GET A WORD.
/	DCA I	STO&177+7420		/STORE A WORD.
/	ISZ	SFROM&177+7420		/BUMP TO NEXT WORD TO MOVE.
/	ISZ	STO&177+7420		/BUMP POINTER/COUNTER.
/	JMP	SMVLUP&177+7420		/KEEP GOING UNTIL ALL ARE MOVED.
/	JMP I	S7600&177+7420		/GO START UP A COMPLETE REBOOT.
S7600,	SBOOT				/SYSTEM RESTART ADDRESS.
SFROM,	STARTIT-20			/BLOCK 0000 DATA LOADED HERE.
STO,	SBOOT				/BLOCK 0000 DATA NEEDED HERE.
S7405,	ROMGO				/ADDRESS OF "ROMGO" ROUTINE.
S5671,	JMP I	WRQUAD			/"JMP I WRQUAD" INSTRUCTION VALUE.

/	NOTE: FUTURE RELEASES OF THIS HANDLER MUST INCLUDE A CALL TO THE SYSTEM DEVICE
/	HANDLER FOR THE PURPOSE OF RELOADING BLOCK 0001-0017; THE REBOOT AT 07600
/	["SBOOT"] WILL BE REWORKED TO USE THE ROM-BASED BOOTUP ROUTINE.

	ZBLOCK	-.			/EMPTY SPACE.

	RELOC				/TURN RELOCATION OFF.
/	SLURP LOADER FOR TD8E WITH MR8E-C ROM.

	NOPUNCH				/FOR NOW.

	*7600				/WHERE THIS EXECUTES.

	ENPUNCH				/FOR NOW.

SBOOT,	IOF				/TURN INTERRUPTS OFF.
SL7670,	-110				/CONSTANT 7670; THIS CLEARS THE AC.
SLROMAD,ROMADR				/ENTRY POINT INTO THE ROM TO REBOOT; THIS
					/WILL NOT SKIP BECAUSE THE AC IS CLEAR.
					/HOWEVER, IT MAY BE SKIPPED DEPENDING ON THE
					/PRIOR CONTENTS OF THE AC.
	CIF	ROMFLD			/GOING TO ROM FIELD.
	JMP I	SLROMADR/(ROMADR)	/GO TO BOOTUP ROUTINE.

	SLBTEND=.			/ACTUAL END OF BOOTSTRAP-REQUIRED CODE.

/	NOTE: AS OF VERSION 8Z, THERE IS AN SPECIFIC UPPER LIMIT ON THE SIZE OF THE
/	CODE NEEDED TO REBOOT P?S/8 WHEN REMOVED FROM THE SLURP LOADER [TO BE USED
/	WITH THE P?S/8 VERSIONS OF THE BIN AND RIM LOADERS].  VARIOUS EARLIER RELEASES
/	MAY HAVE MADE DIFFERENT DEMANDS ON THIS CODE LENGTH [AND VERSION 9A WILL
/	CHANGE THIS UPPER LIMIT TO ONE WORD LESS].  IT IS NOT EXPECTED THIS NEW
/	REQUIREMENT WILL AFFECT TOO MANY SYSTEM CONFIGURATIONS; EACH WILL HAVE TO BE
/	RECODED AS REQUIRED.  HOWEVER, THIS CONFIGURATION USES ONE OF THE SMALLEST
/	BOOTUP SECTIONS; AS SUCH, NO CHANGES WILL BE NEEDED FOR THE P?S/8 TD8E WITH
/	MR8E-C ROM VARIANT.  [NOTE: THE TC01/TC08 SYSTEM, ONCE REASSEMBLED FOR USE
/	WITH VERSION 9A, IS ONE WORD SHORTER THAN THE NEW LIMITATION.  EACH SYSTEM
/	DEVICE HANDLER WILL BE EVALUATED REGARDING THIS POINT, ETC.]
